 # Stackless Traversal
 
-Also called: Algorithme sans pile, Parcours sans pile
+Also called: Algorithme sans pile, Parcours sans pile, Parent-link traversal, Stack-less Tree Traversal
 
 ## Overview
-Stackless Traversal is a method for traversing hierarchical volume structures (specifically N3-trees) that eliminates the need for a stack data structure by recalculating Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) parameters at each tree descent and ascent [S1, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods like [Leaf Collection](899-leaf-collection.md) and [Point Plane Test Traversal](982-point-plane-test-traversal.md) by relying on parent pointers for ascent and full DDA recalculation rather than incremental updates or explicit leaf enumeration, optimizing for GPU register usage and branch divergence [S1, unofficial].
+Stackless Traversal is a hierarchical volume rendering method that traverses tree structures (specifically N3-trees) without a stack data structure by recalculating Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) parameters at each tree descent and ascent [S1, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods like [Hierarchical Trilinear Ray Casting](851-hierarchical-trilinear-ray-casting.md) and [Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) Traversal](3061-digital-differential-analyzer-dda-traversal.md) by relying on explicit parent pointers for upward navigation and full DDA recalculation rather than incremental updates or implicit stack management, optimizing for GPU register pressure and branch divergence [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** A hierarchical volume structure (N3-tree) where each node stores a pointer to its parent and, if non-empty, an average color/value and occupancy status. A ray defined by origin and direction.
-**Outputs:** Integrated color and opacity for the ray.
+**Inputs:** A hierarchical volume structure (N3-tree) where each node stores a pointer to its parent and, if non-empty, an average color/value and occupancy status [S1, unofficial]. A ray defined by origin and direction [S1, unofficial].
+**Outputs:** Integrated color and opacity for the ray [S1, unofficial].
 
 **Data Structures:**
-*   **Node:** Contains a pointer to the parent node, a pointer to child nodes (if internal), and metadata (average color, occupancy).
-*   **DDA State:** Current position, step size, and direction signs for the current voxel/brick.
